    }
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is AI search optimisation?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "AI search optimisation (also referred to as AEO, GEO, or LLM SEO) is the discipline of ensuring your business is visible and citable by AI-powered search engines, including ChatGPT, Google AI Overviews, Perplexity, Claude, and Microsoft Copilot. It centres on entity authority, structured data, citation development, and content formatting that AI systems can parse and attribute to your business. The objective is not to rank within a list of links but to be cited within AI-generated answers." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How does AEO differ from traditional SEO?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Traditional SEO is concerned with ranking your website within Google's blue link results. AEO (Answer Engine Optimisation) is concerned with securing citations within AI-generated answers. The techniques overlap: structured data, quality content, and authority signals are relevant to both. However, AEO additionally requires entity strategy, llms.txt implementation, AI crawler configuration, and citation monitoring across multiple AI platforms. Both are necessary for maximum visibility." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Which AI search engines are most significant?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Google AI Overviews commands the largest reach because it appears directly within Google search results. ChatGPT Search and Perplexity are the most widely adopted standalone AI search tools. Microsoft Copilot holds significance for enterprise users owing to its integration into Microsoft 365 and Edge. Claude and Apple Intelligence continue to grow. A thorough strategy addresses all six platforms." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How can I determine whether my business appears in ChatGPT?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Open ChatGPT with web browsing enabled and request that it recommend businesses within your category in Reading. For instance, ask \"Who are the best accountants in Reading?\" or \"Recommend an IT support company near Thames Valley Park.\" If your business is not referenced, you have an AI visibility gap. Repeat this across Perplexity, Copilot, and Claude for a comprehensive picture. Results vary between platforms and sessions, so test multiple times." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is llms.txt?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "llms.txt is a plain text file placed at your website's root (comparable to robots.txt) that provides AI crawlers with a structured summary of your site's content, services, and key information. It adheres to the open specification at llmstxt.org. The file assists AI systems in understanding your business quickly and accurately, increasing the likelihood of correct citations. It is straightforward to create, easy to maintain, and increasingly expected by AI crawlers." }
      },
      {
